# Build context for rsk/Dockerfile (the only build using context ".").
#
# Allowlist, because the repo root holds ~4.5 GB the image build never reads
# (grafana/, bench/, .venv/, nogit/, docker volumes) and every per-node rebuild
# would otherwise transfer all of it.
#
# rsk/Dockerfile reads exactly three paths from the context:
#   repos/rskj   -> compiled by Gradle inside the image
#   rsk/         -> genesis files, rsk.conf, logback.xml, jmx agent + config
#   m2/          -> locally built co.rsk:native SNAPSHOT (stage_native_snapshot.sh)
# If you add a COPY to the Dockerfile, allowlist its source here too.
#
# The stats/tools stacks build from subdirectory contexts, so this file does not
# affect them.
*

!repos/rskj
!rsk
!m2

# Untracked runtime data and build output inside repos/rskj. Gradle runs
# `clean build` in the image, so none of this is needed -- and test/ alone is
# ~1.4 GB of regtest database.
repos/rskj/test
repos/rskj/logs
repos/rskj/build
repos/rskj/.gradle
repos/rskj/**/build
repos/rskj/.git

# Never useful in an image build.
**/.DS_Store
